  "source_cause": "The first AddFishCommand invokes the fallback global rec_print_table before queueing SlowlyAppear and AddFishAgain. This global is absent from the independent compatibility installation, so the callback aborts and the subsequent fish command sequence is lost.",
  "change": "Implement the fallback helper with its ordinary table, depth and non-table behavior. Preserve allocated actor userdata semantics for independent actor handles rather than traversing their internal table representation and ownership cycles.",
  "diagnosis": "sweep-2026-10-13-koi-sm-debug-helper-diagnosis.json",
  "regression_control": "A real live owned actor callback covers nil, ordinary nested tables, optional indentation, depth zero with a table cycle, depths one and two, boolean values, real actor ownership cycles, nested actor values, and the following queued command. Native actors have userdata semantics inside this fallback helper.",
